1xx1|n|That one of the four cardinal points directly opposite to the north; the region or direction to the right or direction to the right of a person who faces the east. ; A country, region, or place situated farther to the south than another; the southern section of a country. ; Specifically: That part of the United States which is south of Mason and Dixon's line. See under Line. ; The wind from the south.	N:2ni,98,4;4yp,84,1~2ni,98,4;4yp,84,1
